            "impact": "Regression: previously returned a str such as '/srv/files/foo'; now returns pathlib.Path. Code expecting str may raise TypeError or serialize incorrectly.",
            "explanation": "The diff replaces '/srv/files/' + value with apply(value). The L3 definition of apply shows `return target` where target is created by Path(...).resolve(), so the return type is pathlib.Path, not str. This contradicts the PR claim of preserving externally observable behavior.",
